\f1\fs22 Sarah sat at her pristine desk, in her pristine high-back chair, in her gleaming new office, and stroked the fine-grained, polished timber desktop with such satisfaction, you\'92d think she\'92d inherited a gelato factory. Squaring her shoulders, she readied herself for business, and fired up her quirky little holoscreen. It was an antique device, but the peace she felt when using it \'85 well, that\'92s another story.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Its voice and display reported a table of messages, mostly relating to her previous position. One was about her promotional med-exam, which was at 1:30pm that day. Though a formality, promotions were never confirmed without a clean bill of health. Sarah had never been sick in her life, never so much as a cold. Viruses never affected her. Sarah never sniffled, except in the aftermath of shotgun suicides.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

