\f1\fs22 \'91Ah, Mr Fairy Boxers,\'92 Sarah said as the cleaner appeared at her office door, with his hands clasped at his navel. \'91The scent of your vocation preceded you down the hallway by some seconds.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The cleaner cast about for something he might give voice, and came up with, \'91Sticking with holoscreens are you?\'92 He chuckled. \'91Where\'92s your beta-max?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah rolled her eyes. Her expression posted a message any woman could read, and which every man gormlessly missed: 
\f3\i why do men think insults are good pick-up lines? 
\f1\i0 No one dissed her holoscreen.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What\'92s your name, Mr Fairy Boxers?\'92 she challenged, while still feeling chuffed about her new apartment.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91My name\'92s Tony.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91As in the 
\f3\i Tones
\f1\i0  in SupaTones?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Kinda, yeah.\'92 Tony blushed and his embarrassed smile blushed too.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Fancy yourself a bit of a super singer or something, SupaTones?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tax, no! I don\'92t have a musical bone in my body.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah thought about that and nodded. \'91Good. Mr Fairy Boxers it is then.\'92\
